# Sources with translatable strings, relative to the project source root.
# Every string in them is looked up with T_/TN_ (src/I18n.hpp) under its
# localization-store key id. Keep this list in sync when a source starts (or
# stops) carrying user-facing text: tests/PotfilesTest.cpp fails when a source
# that calls T_ or TN_ is missing here, or when an entry is not such a source.
#
# Read by the maintainer targets po/meson.build sets up (urnetwork-pot and
# urnetwork-update-po run xgettext over it); the build and install never read
# it, since the catalogs come from the localization store.
#
# Not listed, deliberately:
#   src/I18n.hpp        the T_/TN_ wrappers themselves — the only "T_(" text in
#                       it is the documentation comment, not a real call site
#   src/Ui.cpp          stylesheet + widget factories — no user-facing strings
#   src/main.cpp        only the gettext bootstrap and stderr diagnostics
